We will put static methods in the class that is most related to it
if the most related thing is an interface we can also place the static method there.
so when we are going to use a static method?
a public static method will usually be used when the method creates
an object of the class this is called a "factory method"
a good example is a string method like String.format("Hello %s, day %d",
userName, dayNumber)
or String.join(", ", fruitArray)
or String.valueOf(53)
all these create instances of the method
but why not use ctr's for these? because its easier to control
what you want to do since the ctr's name will be the same but using
method names you can control what you desire from the method.

we have Math class which is a collection of static method since each operation works on a arbitrary
object and not some math class object